  "id": "architectshrine",
  "note": "Ten floors of Ascendant devotion that rendered as a three-box stack on the shared asc_shrine arm. Built as a ZIGGURAT: seven square boxes stepping in from the podium to a tenth of its width, with a faceted drum lantern on the apex — the one silhouette in Coldwater that narrows the whole way and ends in a point rather than a lid. ⚠ NO AUTHORED `neon`, deliberately. `derivedStyle` reads `m.neon` as a TRUTH TEST for works-vs-front-vs-block, so authoring a colour here would reclassify a stone shrine as a SHOPFRONT and hang a retail kit on it; the accent it wants (#7fc8ff, off the stone family) is what `accentOf` already derives with the field left empty. RENDER_TUNE.legacyArms puts the asc_shrine arm back.",
